WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.404
From April to June 2026,

2
00:00:02.793 --> 00:00:04.813
India imported 86 billion

3
00:00:04.813 --> 00:00:07.722
dollars more goods than it exported.

4
00:00:07.936 --> 00:00:10.604
Yet its current account deficit

5
00:00:10.604 --> 00:00:12.411
was just 4.2 billion:

6
00:00:12.724 --> 00:00:14.479
half a percent of GDP.

7
00:00:14.726 --> 00:00:16.351
Why? The current account

8
00:00:16.351 --> 00:00:17.977
also counts services and

9
00:00:17.977 --> 00:00:18.654
transfers.

10
00:00:18.907 --> 00:00:22.309
Net services brought in 51.6 billion;

11
00:00:22.598 --> 00:00:25.588
remittance receipts, 42.9 billion.

12
00:00:25.869 --> 00:00:27.718
The other side records investment:

13
00:00:28.049 --> 00:00:30.037
textbooks call it the capital account;

14
00:00:30.374 --> 00:00:33.093
RBI data calls it the financial account.

15
00:00:33.405 --> 00:00:36.183
That quarter, direct investment came in,

16
00:00:36.598 --> 00:00:38.778
while portfolio money flowed out.

17
00:00:39.055 --> 00:00:41.077
Goods tell half the story.

18
00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:43.375
Services and remittances

19
00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:44.488
tell the rest.

20
00:00:44.875 --> 00:00:45.449
Your turn.

21
00:00:45.765 --> 00:00:47.555
Which account records remittances

22
00:00:47.555 --> 00:00:48.206
from abroad?
